------- FILE main.asm
------- FILE midiin.asm LEVEL 2 PASS 3
      0  39d5					      include	"midiin.asm"
      1  39d5							; Fat Chip 64 - MIDI in (Kerberos MIDI IN), v0.11
      2  39d5							;
      3  39d5							; The IRQ (and the main loop's TxService) move each received byte into rxBuf.
      4  39d5							; The main loop parses them (running status; realtime and system bytes are
      5  39d5							; skipped) and plays incoming notes exactly like overlay keys: through the
      6  39d5							; notes mode, latch, arp and K + note.
      7  39d5							;
      8  39d5							; Channels 1-11 are played (any of them, so the keytar's key channel can be
      9  39d5							; anything up to 11). 12-16 are ignored: the Yamaha SHS-10 sends its
     10  39d5							; accompaniment there (chords 12-14, bass 15, drums 16).
     11  39d5							;
     12  39d5							; H / J move incoming notes down / up an octave (-4..+4). A held note keeps
     13  39d5							; its pitch until its note-off, so changing it mid-note can't hang anything.
     14  39d5							;
